<h1>System types</h1>
<p class="muted">Every system is <b>on-grid</b>, <b>off-grid</b> or <b>hybrid</b>. The type decides what is added to the price of a quotation.</p>

<div class="stats">
  <% SystemType::TYPES.each do |key, label| %>
    <div class="stat"><b><%= label %></b><span><%= SystemType::INFO[key] %></span></div>
  <% end %>
</div>
<div class="panel">
  <ul>
    <li><b>On-grid:</b> the battery price is <b>not</b> added to the quotation. A battery added by mistake is left out.</li>
    <li><b>Off-grid:</b> the battery is part of the price, and <b>no subsidy</b> is added.</li>
    <li><b>Hybrid:</b> the battery is part of the price and the subsidy can apply.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<p>
  <% SystemType::TYPES.each do |key, label| %><%= link_to "➕ Build an #{label.downcase} system", admin_new_package_builder_path(type: key), class: "btn go" %> <% end %>
</p>
<%= form_with url: admin_system_types_path, method: :patch do %>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table>
    <tr><th>System</th><th class="right">Capacity</th><th class="right">Price</th><th>Has a battery in its parts?</th><th>Type</th><th></th></tr>
    <% @packages.each do |p| %>
      <tr>
        <td><b><%= p.name %></b></td>
        <td class="right"><%= format("%g", p.capacity_kw.to_f) %> kW</td>
        <td class="right"><%= inr(p.price) %></td>
        <td><%= @with_battery.include?(p.id) ? "Yes" : "No" %></td>
        <td><%= select_tag "types[#{p.id}]", options_for_select(SystemType::TYPES.map { |key, label| [label, key] }, p.system_type) %></td>
        <td><%= link_to "Change parts", admin_edit_package_builder_path(p) %></td>
      </tr>
    <% end %>
    <% if @packages.empty? %><tr><td colspan="6" class="muted">No systems yet. Use “Build a system” above.</td></tr><% end %>
  </table></div>
  <p><%= submit_tag "Save the types", class: "btn go" %></p>
<% end %>
<p class="muted small">A system with a battery in its parts cannot be on-grid: take the battery out under Systems first. A custom quotation (made from parts) is on-grid without a battery, hybrid with a battery and the subsidy, and off-grid with a battery and no subsidy.</p>
